# Physics receipt (P4): drag under every law. The node the boot selects is
# pressed, moved 220 world units right, and released; `drag-return-world` is how far the law
# has since carried it off the drop point. A law that rests reclaims the node
# (the springs pull it home); a restless law keeps moving instead; Still holds
# it exactly where it was let go.
# In world units (ruled 2026-10-04, "Measure in world units"): the gesture and
# every drag-return read the same to the law at any zoom the following view
# reaches, and exactly as the px forms did at zoom 1.
assert title GRAPHSHELL H3 READY
assert snap ready == true
click role:button @data-command=physics:toggle
settle 1
assert snap physics-paused == false
click role:combobox Arrangement
settle 1
click role:option Free (physics alone)
settle 1
click role:button Apply arrangement
settle 1
assert snap layout == free

# --- Springs ---
log drag Springs
click role:combobox Physics law
settle 1
click role:option Springs
settle 1
click role:button Apply physics
settle 120
act select-web
settle 1
assert snap physics-law == spring.rapier
press-focused
settle 1
# The press took hold of a node (a member id, so it carries a dash).
assert snap dragging-node ~ -
move-by-world 220 0
settle 1
release-at
settle 1
assert snap drag-return-world <= 20
settle 300
assert snap drag-return-world >= 40
assert snap layout-overlaps == 0
capture physics_drag_springs_reclaimed
wait

